        {
          "page": "10",
          "section": "5. Conclusion",
          "quote": "Refractory metal high-entropy alloys have been reported to provide performance advantages over conventional alternatives, however their suitability for high temperature service has not been thoroughly characterized within the literature. This study reported on the elevated temperature performance of AlMo0.5NbTa0.5TiZr, which is the archetypal alloy in this class.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "37b8de15bddb610a:part:002"
        }
      ]
